<title>GREECE: Fishing boats shut main Greek port over fuel.</title>
<headline>Fishing boats shut main Greek port over fuel.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fishermen blocked Greece's main passenger port at Piraeus with their boats on Wednesday, stopping all ships from leaving or entering to protest against fuel prices, police said.</p>
<p>About 50 fishing boats stopped the traffic, refusing to budge and demanding a previous tax exemption for fuel prices be restored.</p>
<p>Police said it was unclear when the fishermen would lift the blockade of the port, southwest of Athens.</p>
</text>
